# Project foundation

## What this repository is

The public website for **Auralink Studio** (https://auralinkstudio.com): an agency marketing site, portfolio, educational resource, and lead-generation site. It must explain services clearly, demonstrate expertise, present genuine work, answer prospective clients' questions, and encourage qualified inquiries.

- Services offered: custom static websites; WordPress development; Shopify development; email design and development; lifecycle email marketing and automation; SEO; answer engine optimization (AEO); generative engine optimization (GEO).
- Audience: business owners and marketing teams seeking a professional website, stronger online visibility, ecommerce support, or better email marketing.
- WordPress and Shopify are services sold to clients. This site runs on Astro and never depends on them at runtime.
- The planned information architecture, content types, and content rules live in `docs/content-strategy.md`. Pages are created when their content is ready, not as empty placeholders.

## Stack (exact versions: docs/architecture.md)

| Layer | Choice | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Framework | Astro 7, static output | No adapter. Netlify hosts the `dist/` build. |
| Language | TypeScript, `astro/tsconfigs/strict` | `@/*` maps to `src/*`. |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS 4 via `@tailwindcss/vite` + daisyUI 5 | CSS-first config in `src/styles/global.css`. No `tailwind.config.js`. |
| Interactivity | Vue 3 `<script setup>` islands via `@astrojs/vue` | Only where real client-side state exists. |
| Effects | Selected Inspira UI components (copied into `src/components/inspira/`) | Purposeful, sparing, reduced-motion aware. |
| Content | Astro content collections, Markdown in `src/content/` | Schemas in `src/content.config.ts`. |
| Testing | Playwright + axe-core | `tests/e2e/`. |
| Hosting/forms | Netlify (static) and Netlify Forms | `netlify.toml`. |

## Boundaries

- Do not add React, Next.js, Nuxt, a second CSS framework, a database, authentication, CMS runtime, or an application backend. If a feature seems to need one, stop and explain the requirement instead.
- npm is the package manager. `package-lock.json` is the only lockfile. Do not add another lockfile or switch managers.
- Do not upgrade existing packages across major versions as part of a feature task. Propose migrations separately with the breaking changes listed.
- Prefer stable releases. No prerelease, canary, or nightly packages.
- Keep production dependencies limited to what the build needs; tooling goes in `devDependencies`.

## Repository map

```
src/
  pages/            routes (.astro); dynamic routes read content collections or the typed data in src/data
  layouts/          BaseLayout.astro owns <head>, metadata, skip link, main landmark
  components/
    ui/             small Astro primitives built on daisyUI classes
    sections/       page sections (hero, service grid, CTA, FAQ list)
    seo/            structured data and metadata helpers
    islands/        Vue 3 interactive components (hydrated)
    inspira/        Inspira UI components copied in and adapted
  content/          Markdown collections: services, work, insights, faqs
  content.config.ts collection schemas (Zod)
  data/site.ts      verified business facts, service catalogue, service cards, planned routes
  data/detail-pages.ts, data/service-pages/, data/industry-pages/
                    typed, proposed copy of the nine service and sixteen industry detail pages
  lib/              utils.ts cn() class merger, icons.ts icon set, service-cards.ts card links
  styles/global.css Tailwind + daisyUI + tokens
  assets/           images processed by astro:assets
public/             files served as-is (favicons, robots.txt)
tests/e2e/          Playwright suites (smoke, a11y, motion, navigation, hero, seo, layout, rendering)
scripts/            executable checks (workflow, content, Lighthouse audit)
docs/               architecture, content strategy, quality checks, SEO/AEO/GEO, performance
reports/            generated screenshots and Lighthouse reports (gitignored)
design/             editable source artwork for generated images (hero-mockup, process-lines)
.cursor/            rules, agents, skills (this instruction system)
```

## Content integrity

Never invent client names, logos, testimonials, certifications, pricing, statistics, outcomes, or performance claims. Verified facts live only in `src/data/site.ts` and `docs/content-strategy.md`; everything else stays `draft: true` and is labelled as proposed. Workflow, commands, and the guidance index are in `AGENTS.md` (loaded with this rule) and `.cursor/rules/development-workflow.mdc`.
